### Marketplace — the digital-asset marketplace (openspec:
### add-digital-asset-marketplace). The catalog and product pages are Blazor
### (Components/Pages/Marketplace/), not a JSON API — browse them at
### {{baseUrl}}/marketplace. The only HTTP endpoint the feature adds is the
### Stripe webhook.

@baseUrl = https://localhost:7105

### Stripe webhook — Endpoints/StripeWebhookEndpoints.cs
### POST /api/stripe/webhook. Unauthenticated and antiforgery-disabled: the
### Stripe-Signature header IS the authentication. A body without a valid
### signature (like this one) is rejected 400 and changes nothing.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/stripe/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": "evt_test", "type": "payment_intent.succeeded", "data": { "object": { "id": "pi_test" } } }

### A real event needs the signature Stripe computes over "{timestamp}.{body}"
### with the endpoint's signing secret. Locally, forward real events with the
### Stripe CLI (it prints the whsec_… to put in Stripe:WebhookSecret):
###
###   stripe listen --forward-to https://localhost:7105/api/stripe/webhook
###   stripe trigger payment_intent.succeeded
###
### The handler is idempotent per Stripe event id (ProcessedWebhookEvents) and
### per payment-intent id (StripePayments), and only advances a purchase from
### Pending → Paid.
